# Running Tests

```bash
nvm use
npm test
```

Runs `mocha test/**/*.test.js`. All 70 tests should pass in ~130ms.

## Structure

- `test/jobSteps/` — job step unit tests
- `test/helpers/` — helper function tests
- `test/util/` — utility tests
- `test/mocks/` — SFCC `dw.*` API stubs (used via `proxyquire`)
- `test/examples/` — mock usage reference

## Notes

- Test files use `.test.js` suffix only (no `.spec.js`)
- SFCC APIs (`dw.*`) are never available in Node — always mock them via `test/mocks/`
- `triggerFileImport` and other private module functions are not tested directly; test via exported step functions (`beforeStep`, `afterStep`, etc.)
